3:T1118,<h2>Introduction</h2>
<p>Frozen shoulder, or adhesive capsulitis, is a condition that causes pain and stiffness in the shoulder joint. Over time, the shoulder can become very difficult to move, significantly impacting daily life. Residents of Hyderabad looking for solutions to relieve this painful condition can find expert care with exercises for frozen shoulder and recovery plans tailored by specialists. At Apollo Hospitals, Financial District, Hyderabad, Dr. B Harsha Vardhana Reddy offers comprehensive orthopedic care to guide you through recovery.</p>

<h2>Understanding Frozen Shoulder</h2>
<p>Frozen shoulder typically develops in stages: the freezing stage (pain worsens, and the shoulder loses range of motion), the frozen stage (pain may reduce, but stiffness remains), and the thawing stage (gradual return to normal range of motion). Diagnosis often involves a physical examination and imaging tests like X-rays or MRIs to rule out other conditions such as arthritis.</p>

<h2>Exercises for Frozen Shoulder</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Warm-Up Exercises:</strong> Before engaging in stretching exercises, warm up your shoulder with activities like pendulum swings to increase blood flow and flexibility. Simply lean over slightly and allow your arm to swing gently back and forth.</li>
    <li><strong>Stretching Exercises:</strong> Try the towel stretch by holding a towel behind your back and using your unaffected arm to gently pull the towel upwards, stretching your frozen shoulder.</li>
    <li><strong>Cross-Body Reach:</strong> Use your unaffected arm to lift the affected arm at the elbow, bringing it across your body to stretch the shoulder.</li>
    <li><strong>Strengthening Exercises:</strong> Incorporate isometric shoulder rotations into your routine by using a wall for resistance to help rebuild shoulder strength gradually.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Treatment Options</h2>
<p>Managing frozen shoulder typically involves a combination of home exercises, physical therapy, and in some cases, medication or intervention. At Apollo Hospitals, Financial District, Hyderabad, Dr. B Harsha Vardhana Reddy provides individualized orthopaedic treatment plans, which may include:</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Physical Therapy:</strong> Specialized stretching exercises and manual therapy to improve mobility.</li>
    <li><strong>Medications:</strong> Pain relievers and anti-inflammatory medications to manage discomfort.</li>
    <li><strong>Steroid Injections:</strong> To reduce inflammation and relieve pain.</li>
    <li><strong>Surgical Intervention:</strong> In severe cases, procedures such as shoulder arthroscopy can help release the tightened joint capsule.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Why Choose Dr. Harsha at Apollo Hospitals, Hyderabad?</h2>
<p>When it comes to treating frozen shoulder in Hyderabad, Dr. B Harsha Vardhana Reddy at Apollo Hospitals, Financial District, Hyderabad, is a highly respected Senior Consultant Orthopedic Surgeon. Dr. Harsha is dedicated to providing patient-centered care, using the latest medical advancements to ensure effective recovery. His expertise in orthopedic surgery and commitment to personalized patient care make him a preferred choice for individuals seeking relief from shoulder conditions.</p>

<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<p><strong>Q: How long does it take to recover from a frozen shoulder?</strong></p>
<p>A: Recovery can vary, but most people recover in about 1 to 3 years. A consistent exercise regimen, as advised by your healthcare provider, can significantly aid recovery.</p>

<p><strong>Q: Is it safe to perform exercises with a frozen shoulder?</strong></p>
<p>A: Yes, but it is important to follow an approved exercise plan to avoid further injury. Consult with an orthopedic expert to ensure your exercises are safe and effective.</p>

<p><strong>Q: When should I see a doctor for my frozen shoulder?</strong></p>
<p>A: If you experience persistent pain and stiffness in your shoulder, it is advisable to consult a healthcare professional for a full evaluation and customized treatment plan.</p>

<h2>Book Your Appointment</h2>
<p>Call Dr. Harsha at <strong>+91 99599 64567</strong> or visit Apollo Hospitals, Financial District, Nanakramguda, Hyderabad. With specialized care and advanced treatment options, you can start your journey towards pain-free mobility and an improved quality of life.</p>5:["slug","frozen-shoulder-exercises-and-recovery-hyderabad","d"]
